# podcast-transcribe .env. install.sh copies this to the node's project dir
# (mode 600, owned by the daemon's user) when there is none, and never
# overwrites it. Edit, then reload:
#   Mac:       sudo -u _wharf vi /opt/wharf/projects/podcast-transcribe/.env
#              sudo -u _wharf /opt/wharf/bin/wharf reload-projects
#   stereo-au: sudo -u wharf vi /srv/wharf/projects/podcast-transcribe/.env
#              sudo /srv/wharf/bin/wharf reload-projects
# (wharfd reads .env when it loads the project.) The node runs
# WHARF_ENV_PASSTHROUGH=strict: only the keys below reach the handler.
# Placeholders only: never commit a filled-in copy.

# Enables the LLM step (ad labels, and chapters when the publisher has none),
# via OpenRouter. Without it jobs still complete and a wantLlm result says
# llm / llmError: "skipped: no OPENROUTER_API_KEY".
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter model slug. Default anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=

# Thinking: low (default) | medium | high | off | default (the model's own).
# anthropic/* can't turn thinking off (off = low there). On
# google/gemini-3.8-flash, low means ZERO thinking and over-consolidated
# chapters, and leaving Gemini at its default makes thinking dominate cost.
# OPENROUTER_REASONING=

# The node's shared whisper models. install.sh fills this in when it creates
# .env: /opt/wharf/share/whisper on the Mac, /usr/local/share/whisper on
# stereo-au. The project's data/models/ is searched after it.
WHISPER_MODEL_DIR=

# Model overrides: a name (tiny.en, base.en, large-v3-turbo) looked up in the
# dirs above, or an absolute path to a ggml .bin. Unset = the per-node
# defaults (README "Which model"): the Mac uses base.en to align and
# large-v3-turbo when listeners read whisper's transcript; CPU nodes use
# tiny.en and base.en. WHISPER_MODEL applies to every job, WHISPER_MODEL_READ
# only to jobs with no publisher transcript.
# WHISPER_MODEL=
# WHISPER_MODEL_READ=
